\title{Reading the Lean proof alongside the paper}
\taxon{Overview}
\meta{dependencies}{None.}
\meta{provenance}{Expository organization and source review, 9 October 2026.}

\p{Start with [the theorem's Lean entry point](/source-material/openai-math/lean/OAI/Combinatorics/Crossing/Main.lean). The main declaration is OAI.Zarankiewicz.mainTarget_proof. Its conclusion combines an explicit drawing attaining the claimed count with a lower bound for every admissible drawing. The companion ordinary_crossing_number_eq then identifies the infimum with that value.}

\p{The following table is a route through the [pinned Lean sources](cn-0059). The two topology lemmas are in the namespace OAI.Zarankiewicz.TruncatedSpokeCoordinates; most other declarations are in OAI.Zarankiewicz. Source files expose their full namespaces and hypotheses.}

